            <ArticleTitle>Usefulness of positive troponin-T and negative creatine kinase levels in identifying high-risk patients with unstable angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>510-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Troponin-T was measured in patients with chest pain and negative creatine phosphokinase-MB isoenzymes. Patients with elevated troponin-T had a significantly greater risk of cardiac events over the next 6 months than patients with normal troponin-T.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
